        <mxCell id="c4" value="Off-peak, 21:00&#10;DepthFirst" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F7FAFD;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1110" y="270" width="340" height="50" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="zFlow" value="FLOWS AND DESIGN NOTES" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F7FAFD;strokeColor=#1F5B96;strokeWidth=1.5;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F5B96;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="360" width="1420" height="255" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f0" value="1  Two independent azurerm_virtual_desktop_scaling_plan resources - not one plan applied to both host pools" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="400" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f1" value="2  centralus ramps up an hour earlier and ramps down an hour earlier than eastus2 - genuinely different demand assumptions, not a copy" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#B77300;fontSize=11;fontColor=#B77300;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="440" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f2" value="3  Each plan's host_pool_association scopes it to exactly one region's host pool - a scaling event in one region cannot affect the other" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="480" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3" value="4  A VM tagged with the autoscale_exclusion_tag_name value is skipped by that region's plan entirely, regardless of schedule phase" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="520" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f4" value="5  Start VM on Connect (set on both host pools in Lab 14) lets a user reach a deallocated host outside its scaling plan's ramp-up window" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#243A5E;fontSize=11;fontColor=#243A5E;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="560" width="1380" height="32" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="foot" value="Original architecture diagram created for this book. Not a Microsoft diagram. Verified against terraform/lab17-regional-autoscaling, August 2026. Self-contained shapes, no remote icon dependency." style="text;fontSize=10;fontColor=#605E5C;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="635" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
